     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: (1) Civil Works Progress: The design-and-build contract for the main road was awarded on 10 October 2012; work commencement on 9 November 2012. As of March 2016, all major original works were almost completed. In December 2015, ADB approved extension of the civil works contract from 9 November 2015 to 31 July 2016 to allow completion of minor outstanding works, as well as rehabilitation of two additional bridges in Dupula and Urmitan. In May 2016, ADB approved another variation order to the main civil work contract to cover, among others, additional works (construction of the gallery) to improve operational characteristics of the road and increase the safety of road users. ADB also approved further extension of the main civil works contract until 31 January 2017. Rehabilitation works have been completed.

(2) Improved road safety: Contract for procurement of road maintenance equipment was signed on 10 June 2015; equipment was delivered in the first quarter 2016. The draft National Road Strategy and Action Plan was submitted to EA for review and comments in August 2015 and approved by MOT on 15 September 2015. Implementation of the Action plan is being completed.

(3) Feeder road improvement and maintenance: Two separate contracts for rehabilitation and improvement of rural roads in Ayni and Panjakent districts were awarded in June 2015. Rehabilitation works started in August 2015 and completed by 30 November 2016.

(4) Border post infrastructure upgrading: The works at Sarazm custom border post comprise the design and construction of an administrative building, customs control building (terminal), canteen, storehouses, checkpoints, bus scanner shelters, toilet buildings, dog cages, disinfection barrier, and asphalted light vehicles parking and other vehicle transit and movement areas, street lighting, landscaping etc. and other associated works including internal and external engineering services. The contract for Sarazm Border Infrastructure Improvement was awarded on 16 October 2015. The works started in November 2015 and were completed in October 2016.</narrative>
